            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for the moment that, then the Persian for by chance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: اتفاق افتادن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اتفاق افتادن (ettefâq oftâdan) — \"to happen\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دیشب در خیابان ما یک اتفاق عجیب افتاد. Dishab dar khiyâbân-e mâ yek ettefâq-e 'ajib oftâd. Last night something strange happened in our street."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally \"an event falls\". Present stem oft-: in ziyâd ettefâq mioftad \"this happens a lot\". Che ettefâqi oftâd? \"What happened?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun ettefâq is borrowed from Arabic ittifāq (EtymDB). The verb oftâdan \"to fall\" is inherited Persian, so the phrase is a Persian compound verb built on an Arabic noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
