          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به وقوع پیوستن (be voqu' peyvastan) — \"to come about, to take place (formal)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "این اتفاق دو سال پیش به وقوع پیوست. In ettefâq do sâl pish be voqu' peyvast. This came about two years ago."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Very formal: news and history writing. voqu' \"occurrence\" + peyvastan \"to join\"; present stem peyvand-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "voqu' is usually traced to Arabic wuqū', \"a falling, an occurrence\"; EtymDB lists no entry. peyvastan \"to join\" is inherited from Middle Persian paywastan (EtymDB). Literally \"to join with occurrence\"."
            }
          ]
        },
