          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دوام آوردن (davâm âvardan) — \"to last, to hold out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سقف خانه زیر برف سنگین دوام نیاورد. Saqf-e khâne zir-e barf-e sangin davâm nayâvard. The roof of the house did not hold out under the heavy snow."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally \"to bring durability\". Present stem âvar-: davâm miâvarad; the negative past is davâm nayâvard."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "davâm \"duration, lasting\" is borrowed from Arabic dawām; EtymDB lists the Arabic word, though not the Persian one. âvardan \"to bring\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
